% sample.web -- a tiny literate program, so that `tangle' and `weave' can% be shown doing their job.  WEB is Knuth's literate-programming language:% one source, from which TANGLE makes the Pascal a compiler reads and WEAVE% makes the TeX a person reads.%%   tangle /dd/DOC/tex/sample.web      writes sample.p, the Pascal%   weave  /dd/DOC/tex/sample.web      writes sample.tex, the document%% Both write into the DATA directory.  Added 2026-08-31; before it, the% gallery card for these two was a photograph of their usage lines, because% no .web file was anywhere on the disk.\datethis@* A tiny program.This is the smallest thing that is still a WEB program: a section of prose,a definition, and the Pascal that comes out the other end.@d greeting=='hello from WEB'@p program sample(output);begin  write(greeting);  writeln;end.@* Index.